  (text "PRELIM - ADXL354 single-ended front end into the ADAU1861.\nPer docs/sensor-head-design-note.md and\ndocs/audio-board-decision-record.md (Decision B: ADAU1861\nruled, ADAU1372 rejected for this board).\n\nWIRED: ADAU1861 full power tree (1V8/AGND) + boot straps\n(PD, SELFBOOT, ROM_BOOT_MODE, REG_EN - tied to safe\ndefaults, [assumed], not checked against UG-2257's boot\nsection yet). ADXL354 X/Y/Z -> 100nF C0G coupling ->\n1Mohm bias to buffered CM -> LTC6242 unity-gain buffers\n-> AINN0/1/2, single-ended (AINP0/1/2 tied to raw CM).\n4th LTC6242 unit buffers CM per design note S6.\nIM72D128V PDM mic -> DMIC01/DMIC_CLK on U1, per design\nnote S8 (digital-only, no coupling/buffer). VDD on 1V8\nwith 1uF bypass per datasheet footnote 3; LR tied to\nAGND (DATA1 channel). DMIC23/MP2 (2nd mic pair) marked\nno-connect - this board carries one mic.\n\nAD2428 (U5) PLACED for future A2B connection to the\nearcups, per docs/audio-board-decision-record.md Decision\nC - this is the A2B bus MASTER node, host side. Only the\nchip's own regulator/decoupling network is wired: VIN's\non-chip LDOs -> VOUT1 (1.9V) -> DVDD/PLLVDD with 4.7uF\nper datasheet p.27; VOUT2 (3.3V) -> ATRXVDD/BTRXVDD with\n4.7uF plus a shared 100nF+10nF per datasheet p.26; VSS\nand EPAD -> AGND (EPAD-to-GND is mandatory, not optional).\nPin numbers and all values taken from AD242x Rev. C\nTable 15 / p.26-27, not guessed.\n\nNOT WIRED (deliberately, out of scope this pass):\ncontrol port (I2C/SPI), SAP0/SAP1 digital audio, JTAG,\nUART, IRQ, QSPIM self-boot flash, headphone/line\noutputs, XTAL. Also U5's entire host-facing I2S/TDM\ninterface (BCLK, SYNC, DTX0/1, DRX0/1, PDMCLK), its I2C\ncontrol port (SCL/SDA/IRQ/ADR1/ADR2), both A2B line pairs\n(AP/AN/ACM towards a master - unused, U5 IS the master;\nBP/BN/BCM towards the first/last slave), SWP/VSSN/SENSE\n(bus power-forwarding to the cups), and IOVDD (needs a\ndomain decision, 3.3V vs 1.8V, before it can be sourced).\nERC's \"not connected\" errors are exactly these pins -\nexpected, not a defect.\n\nOPEN ITEMS (design note S10 + new): buffer-to-AINNx\ncoupling (DC direct vs. footprint a series cap + 0R\njumper) not resolved here. CM pin loading not measured.\nSupply rail \"3V3_ACCEL\" is my judgment call, not in the\nnote - confirm before layout. REG_EN tied low assumes\nDVDD is externally supplied on 1V8, not the internal\nregulator - reasoned, not confirmed against the\ndatasheet's regulator sequencing section. DMIC LR=GND\n(DATA1) is my channel choice, not specified anywhere -\nconfirm against however the DSP expects the PDM stream\nframed.\n\nAD2428 open items, all new: (1) net \"A2B_VIN\" has no\nsource - the datasheet requires 3.7-9.0V AT THE VIN PIN\n(Table 15 p.9), and this board has no rail above 3V3\ntoday. A real supply (5V? higher?) is undesigned.\n(2) IOVDD is left unconnected on purpose - it can run\n3.3V or 1.8V (Operating Conditions p.8); picking 3.3V\nwould let U5 talk to RP1 without the translators Decision\nD mandates for the 1861, but that is my reading, not a\nruling. (3) The A2B bus-coupling network (common-mode\nchoke, AC-coupling caps, diodes D1/D3, VSSN bias inductor)\nis explicitly \"contact your local Analog Devices rep for\nthe latest schematic recommendations\" per datasheet p.33\n- decision record S6 item 3 already flags needing the\nEVAL-AD2428WG1BZ; I have not invented this circuit.\n(4) Whether the cups are bus-powered over A2B or locally\npowered decides SWP/VSSN/SENSE, and is not decided\nanywhere I can find. (5) Upstream channel subset (S4 -\nRev G wants 6, the RP1 link carries 4) still unmade."
    (at 100 215 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)))
    (uuid "fa028809-bee6-4142-8720-7f83e0b64cea")
  )
